infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Head vs tail sampling: where the keep-or-drop decision happens
  desc Decide at the trace root — cheap but blind — or after the trace completes — keeping errors and outliers at the price of a collector
  compares
    - label Head sampling (at the SDK)
      children
        - label Decides at the trace root
          desc ParentBased(TraceIdRatioBased(0.1)) — keep-or-drop is fixed when the trace starts
        - label Nearly free
          desc No buffering and no extra component to run
        - label Blind to what matters
          desc Drops error and slow traces at the same rate as healthy ones
        - label Loses the 03:00 incident
          desc The p95 spike lands inside the 90% already thrown away
    - label Tail sampling (in a collector)
      children
        - label Decides after the trace completes
          desc Buffer the whole trace, then judge it on what actually happened
        - label Keeps errors and outliers
          desc All error traces plus everything past the latency threshold plus a thin baseline
        - label Costs collector memory
          desc Holds every in-flight trace for a 10-30s window — thousands buffered at 600 rps
        - label One more component to run
          desc You operate and scale a collector; the cost is operational, not the bill
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6
